      {
        "id": 194358,
        "name": "Nepycros",
        "username": "Nepycros",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/8491ac/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-04-01T02:48:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had a situation where I was playing in the Multiplayer for the Weekly One-Shot #4: Target Rich Environment with someone I've unfortunately not remembered the name of.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Over the course of the game, we were getting crushed. Everyone except Legacy was brought down, and he was subsequently wrapped up in so many brambles that he couldn't do so much as fight back. Imagine Akash covering the entire environment with so much of herself that every hero is buried and Legacy can barely even keep his head above the dirt. Brought down to 2 HP, we were certain it was over.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But we pressed on, and happened to discover an amazing combo. Even if he couldn't deal damage, even if there was no chance of fighting back by ourselves, we still utilized every resource we had. We had Tempest use his incap power to cycle Take Down back into Legacy's hand. And after that, Unity's incap power would let him play it. Combined with Danger Sense and the ability to use 2 Next Evolution's per turn (to make himself immune to projectile and melee damage), even Advanced Akash'Bhuta couldn't touch him. In the meantime, abilities that let him draw more cards and build up his field until he was high enough in HP to hold his own made it so that he began to move out of the range of The Final Wasteland's voracious creatures. And at long last, they began to chip away at the Brambles, finally destroying those and freeing Legacy. With the limbs removed from the game via Unforgiving Wasteland, and Akash unable to play more cards, Legacy had to beat her down the old-fashioned way, all the while shrugging off every hit.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>We came away with a Mint, but not after 4 painstaking hours spent struggling to overcome nearly impossible odds. That is definitely a game I'll always remember, which I think fits very nicely in this thread's record of high-stakes games.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:21:30.061Z",
